From fcf2dd2d4cacab520aab471699edeb1a550fb36f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WackyHcky <dessierror@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:48:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Online: PSN for GT Sport and GT7 through shadNet and
 RyGTServer

The NP library (libSceNpAuth.prx, target ryty_np) for online play:
- NpSignaling gets a P2P transport in RyGT's libSceNet and resolves peers
  through RyGTServer (ryty_np_p2p.cpp); players register there.
- The web API's HTTP/2 goes out through the game's libSceHttp; PSN calls
  shadNet does not answer (communication restriction status, profanity
  filter, game/player sessions, matches) go to RyGTServer as /rygt/psn/...
  (online_server in RyGT.ini).
- Web API user contexts initialize; push context IDs are real UUID
  strings (games keep them as text); GetPushContext no longer leaves the
  context locked when the ID is unknown; responses report their size.
- sceNpGetAccountLanguage2; GT7's game log (game_log=1 in RyGT.ini).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
